=== DECISIONS ===
Phase-43 forward-ports the React SPA onto the Tesla Fleet Telemetry SI pipeline
delivered by phase-42 (ADR-004, normalize.Pipeline, signal.Store L1 + Redis L2 +
signal_log durable history, generated proto enums, tesla_* prefixed tables).
Public API URLs (/vehicles, /charging, /drives, /analytics/*, /signals/*) are
preserved; response shapes use SI canonical units (meters, m/s, degC, kPa,
joules) and field names match the regenerated proto-derived Go structs.

The following six decisions are LOCKED for the duration of phase-43 and govern
every subsequent prompt (0001+):

1. Forward-port only.
   Every page, route, component, and hook that exists at phase-43 start MUST
   exist at phase-43 end. NO deletions of user-facing surface without explicit
   per-case user approval surfaced as STATUS=BLOCKED on the prompt that wants
   to delete it. Refactoring file paths is allowed; removing functionality is
   not. The audit prompts in this phase enforce this by counting routes,
   pages, hooks, and i18n keys at start vs end.

2. SI everywhere.
   Frontend code assumes SI canonical units from the API and converts to the
   user's preferred display units only at the render boundary via
   web/src/lib/unitConversion.ts. Hooks (web/src/api/hooks/*) MUST NOT mutate,
   round, or convert values. lib/unitConversion.ts MUST NOT assume the
   inbound display unit; it converts FROM SI canonical TO display. This
   matches .github/instructions/unit-conversion.instructions.md.

3. Strict-after phase-42.
   This phase requires phase-42-9999v2-final-gate.log to be STATUS=DONE
   EXIT=0 before any prompt 0001+ runs. v2 is the canonical phase-42
   completion log per ADR-004; v1 (phase-42-9999-final-gate.log) remained
   BLOCKED on log-discipline gaps and is superseded. Every phase-43 prompt's
   gate begins by re-asserting this predecessor invariant.

4. Domain-by-domain end-to-end.
   Each of the 19 feature directories under web/src/features/* gets one
   prompt that updates hooks (web/src/api/hooks) -> types
   (web/src/api/types.ts and web/src/types/*) -> pages
   (web/src/features/<domain>/pages/*) -> i18n (web/src/i18n/en.json) ->
   tests, then verifies cd web; npx tsc --noEmit && npm run build && the
   relevant audit script. A domain prompt is DONE only when the full chain
   is green for that domain.

5. Audit-not-prune.
   Phase-43 includes coverage audits for hooks
   (audit-api-hooks-vs-router.mjs), routes (audit-route-coverage.mjs), and
   i18n keys (audit-i18n-coverage.mjs). When an audit finds an orphan
   (frontend hook with no backend route, page with no entry in router,
   i18n key with no usage) the prompt BLOCKs and the resolution is to add
   the missing surface, NOT to silently delete the orphan. Deletions are
   gated decisions, not housekeeping.

6. No raw HTML, no inline styles, no direct recharts/leaflet imports.
   Existing engineering rules from .github/copilot-instructions.md continue
   to apply: shared <Button>/<Input>/<Select>/<Textarea>/<Modal>/<DataTable>
   from @/components/ui; charts via @/components/charts (no
   import { LineChart } from 'recharts'); maps via @/components/maps (no
   import { MapContainer } from 'react-leaflet'); no inline style={{}}
   with static CSS variables; no hardcoded English strings; no double
   /api/v1 prefix in hook URLs; snake_case query params; light-mode parity
   via var(--text-primary)/var(--text-secondary)/var(--text-muted); WCAG
   2.5.5/2.5.8 touch-target floor of >=24x24. The audit gate enforces
   these on every domain prompt.

These six decisions are not negotiable within phase-43. A prompt that wants
to bend any of them MUST STOP and surface STATUS=BLOCKED with a clear
explanation; the user (not the agent) decides whether to amend ADR-004 or
override the lock.

